1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:53,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:00,710
Do we really have to break up?

3
00:01:06,173 --> 00:01:07,730
I don’t want to do long-distance.

4
00:01:15,802 --> 00:01:17,090
There’s a blank space right here.

5
00:01:22,130 --> 00:01:23,131
Sign it.

6
00:01:34,250 --> 00:01:38,451
[Good luck at your new place, Blue. Love you forever.]

7
00:01:42,462 --> 00:01:43,463
I gotta go.

8
00:02:54,430 --> 00:02:55,470
- Thank you.
- Hey, Blue.

9
00:02:55,899 --> 00:02:56,900
Welcome.

10
00:03:00,322 --> 00:03:01,410
Oh, I missed you so much.

11
00:03:01,458 --> 00:03:03,730
How are you? How are you parents?

12
00:03:04,765 --> 00:03:05,890
They're doing well.

13
00:03:06,210 --> 00:03:07,630
Let me help you with that.

14
00:03:09,293 --> 00:03:10,650
Whose fruit basket is this, Uncle?

15
00:03:11,266 --> 00:03:13,050
Oh, it’s a customer’s basket.

16
00:03:13,154 --> 00:03:15,290
I’m delivering it for your dad.

17
00:03:19,696 --> 00:03:20,697
Got it.

18
00:03:26,867 --> 00:03:29,490
- Is this everything you packed?
- Yeah.

19
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:30,931
Let's go.

20
00:03:34,030 --> 00:03:35,031
You should go now.

21
00:03:36,042 --> 00:03:37,210
I’ll see you off here.

22
00:03:37,912 --> 00:03:40,330
Take good care of yourself, Blue.

23
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:42,531
Thank you,

24
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:45,130
and please tell Mom and Dad not to worry.

25
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:49,531
Let's go.

26
00:03:52,531 --> 00:03:54,010
I’ll show you around your new school.

27
00:03:57,293 --> 00:03:58,294
It's there?

28
00:03:58,381 --> 00:04:00,050
Yeah, just go straight.

29
00:04:02,395 --> 00:04:03,396
I see the sign.

30
00:04:11,336 --> 00:04:12,337
Hey!

31
00:04:13,010 --> 00:04:14,410
Isn’t the dorm this way?

32
00:04:14,930 --> 00:04:17,810
Yeah, but we’re going somewhere else first.

33
00:04:20,709 --> 00:04:22,850
You go on. I can find the dorm myself.

34
00:04:24,674 --> 00:04:25,675
I flunked my exams,

35
00:04:26,222 --> 00:04:28,770
so I have to do community service for the school.

36
00:04:29,042 --> 00:04:32,210
They need two people, and I already signed you up.

37
00:04:33,170 --> 00:04:34,171
Help me out,

38
00:04:34,376 --> 00:04:36,630
and you can have the bottom bunk.

39
00:04:36,685 --> 00:04:37,686
Please, Blue. Please?

40
00:04:58,490 --> 00:05:00,770
[Chantrawattana School Foundation Annual Charity Fair]

41
00:05:03,410 --> 00:05:06,531
Dorm kids are basically their servants,

42
00:05:07,112 --> 00:05:09,290
if they want dorm points anyway. Think of this as practice.

43
00:05:11,101 --> 00:05:13,890
And your parents are okay with you moving to another province?

44
00:05:16,013 --> 00:05:17,934
Mom didn’t really want me to move here,

45
00:05:19,794 --> 00:05:21,970
but when I brought up college,

46
00:05:22,701 --> 00:05:23,770
she couldn’t exactly say no.

47
00:05:25,624 --> 00:05:26,930
And my dad…

48
00:05:29,058 --> 00:05:31,290
I don't know. I guess Mom told him.

49
00:05:56,562 --> 00:05:58,930
Good evening, Mr. Po and Mr. Yi.

50
00:05:59,106 --> 00:06:00,107
Good evening, Director.

51
00:06:00,504 --> 00:06:02,610
I'm sorry I'm late.

52
00:06:02,968 --> 00:06:05,730
You’re not late at all. You arrived just in time.

53
00:06:05,842 --> 00:06:08,130
Tokyo is about to perform.

54
00:06:08,653 --> 00:06:10,654
Why don’t you come sit at the table first?

55
00:06:11,090 --> 00:06:12,091
Please follow me.

56
00:06:19,661 --> 00:06:22,130
Pupe, I told you to go left! Hurry up!

57
00:06:22,296 --> 00:06:23,850
Well, I am!

58
00:06:26,582 --> 00:06:29,790
Tokyo, you’re up next, okay? Your dad’s waiting to see you perform.

59
00:06:31,261 --> 00:06:32,262
Okay, ma'am.

60
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,301
Damn it!

61
00:06:38,713 --> 00:06:39,714
That wasn’t the cue.

62
00:06:40,064 --> 00:06:41,230
It's show time.

63
00:07:08,590 --> 00:07:10,591
[Singing off-key.]

64
00:07:27,745 --> 00:07:30,350
Tokyo’s voice sounds really good today, Mr. Po.

65
00:07:31,089 --> 00:07:32,470
Sounds good, my ass.

66
00:07:33,628 --> 00:07:34,629
Blue, come on.

67
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:36,391
Don’t give in to the voice in your head.

68
00:07:36,950 --> 00:07:38,070
Keep your thoughts to yourself.

69
00:07:38,430 --> 00:07:41,710
That’s Tokyo, one of the Street Queens. Her dad’s a big shot around here.

70
00:07:42,310 --> 00:07:43,820
That guy is Mr. Po,

71
00:07:44,284 --> 00:07:45,285
her dad.

72
00:07:57,030 --> 00:07:59,350
Go handle it. Don’t embarrass us.

73
00:08:00,196 --> 00:08:01,197
Yes, Dad.

74
00:08:19,710 --> 00:08:20,711
Hurry up.

75
00:08:26,534 --> 00:08:27,535
Where the hell is she?

76
00:08:28,188 --> 00:08:29,830
Split up! Don’t let Tokyo escape!

77
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:39,461
Hey, you.

78
00:08:40,630 --> 00:08:41,710
Could you go to the school entrance

79
00:08:42,089 --> 00:08:44,310
and pick up the birthday cake for the guest?

80
00:08:44,692 --> 00:08:45,693
Bring it inside for me, okay?

81
00:08:46,132 --> 00:08:47,133
I can help her.

82
00:08:47,305 --> 00:08:49,390
No need to. The new girl can handle this.

83
00:08:50,724 --> 00:08:51,756
Come on, you're coming with me.

84
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:54,030
We need your help over there. Let’s go.

85
00:08:56,593 --> 00:08:57,594
Hold on.

86
00:09:00,774 --> 00:09:01,775
Is Tokyo inside?

87
00:09:06,422 --> 00:09:07,670
Are you two running away like this?

88
00:09:07,974 --> 00:09:09,070
No, Yi. I'm just…

89
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:11,470
I’m taking the cart to get water for the guests.

90
00:09:11,956 --> 00:09:12,957
Oh, really?

91
00:09:13,190 --> 00:09:14,191
Move, kid.

92
00:09:35,070 --> 00:09:36,471
[With the utmost respect.]

93
00:09:53,401 --> 00:09:54,402
Hey!

94
00:09:57,812 --> 00:09:58,813
Shit!

95
00:10:27,948 --> 00:10:29,630
Am I screwed from day one?

96
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,190
Are you even going to apologize?

97
00:10:41,526 --> 00:10:43,510
Apologize for what? You ran into me.

98
00:10:43,937 --> 00:10:44,938
What?

99
00:10:45,068 --> 00:10:46,150
That’s a pretty messed-up thing to say.

100
00:10:46,910 --> 00:10:47,911
I know.

101
00:10:48,350 --> 00:10:49,351
People called me pretty all the time.

102
00:10:50,924 --> 00:10:52,470
Can’t you just say sorry like a normal person?

103
00:10:53,068 --> 00:10:54,069
Do you have to be such a jerk?

104
00:10:56,110 --> 00:10:57,111
Hey, ladies!

105
00:10:59,172 --> 00:11:00,470
I didn't do it.

106
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:05,031
Follow me.

107
00:11:07,846 --> 00:11:08,847
Okay.

108
00:11:24,870 --> 00:11:26,871
[Singing]

109
00:11:46,817 --> 00:11:47,818
Mr. Po.

110
00:11:48,881 --> 00:11:52,310
A student dropped Chief Tul's cake, sir

111
00:11:56,028 --> 00:11:57,029
Good evening.

112
00:11:59,726 --> 00:12:00,727
Oh, hello.

113
00:12:07,857 --> 00:12:09,110
Good evening, sir.

114
00:12:09,772 --> 00:12:10,773
Good evening.

115
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:12,551
Hope you’re doing well.

116
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:18,790
[With the deepest respect, Wiboon Monchaitrakul]

117
00:12:23,068 --> 00:12:24,069
Oh,

118
00:12:24,590 --> 00:12:27,750
someone dropped by with a gift to congratulate me.

119
00:12:27,897 --> 00:12:28,898
I see.

120
00:12:30,377 --> 00:12:32,430
Actually, I still have many gifts for you,

121
00:12:32,684 --> 00:12:35,790
but they’re currently on their way from Singapore.

122
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:39,150
Once my other son returns to Thailand,

123
00:12:39,329 --> 00:12:41,390
I assure you they’ll be delivered straight to you.

124
00:12:42,364 --> 00:12:45,630
I hope we can continue to count on your kindness.

125
00:12:46,590 --> 00:12:47,591
Thank you.

126
00:12:51,550 --> 00:12:52,830
You know me so well.

127
00:12:55,630 --> 00:12:56,631
This way, please.

128
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:02,370
Is that your daughter?

129
00:13:02,905 --> 00:13:03,910
That's right.

130
00:13:05,670 --> 00:13:06,671
She has a great voice.

131
00:13:06,908 --> 00:13:07,909
Thank you, sir.

132
00:13:17,376 --> 00:13:18,720
You need to soak your clothes first.

133
00:13:20,208 --> 00:13:21,280
Blue!

134
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,920
You’re only supposed to add one scoop.

135
00:13:23,072 --> 00:13:25,080
Are you planning to get these clothes clean by next year or what?

136
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:28,160
Yeah, I’ll wash all this bad luck away once and for all.

137
00:13:29,435 --> 00:13:31,880
I warned you not to mess with Tokyo.

138
00:13:32,784 --> 00:13:34,260
I wasn’t trying to mess with her.

139
00:13:35,232 --> 00:13:36,480
She bumped into me.

140
00:13:38,712 --> 00:13:41,523
And what the hell is wrong with the teachers here?

141
00:13:43,683 --> 00:13:45,520
They don’t even punish the person who started it.

142
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:49,841
Every teacher in this school is obviously taking Tokyo’s side.

143
00:13:50,115 --> 00:13:51,320
Because her last name is Kongpurim.

144
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:54,201
Look over there.

145
00:13:55,048 --> 00:13:56,049
- That’s Mr. Po’s real name.
- [Chaichana Kongpurim]

146
00:13:56,051 --> 00:13:57,360
- [Akeyuth Kongpurim]
- [Charnyuth Kongpurim]

147
00:13:57,798 --> 00:13:59,200
Are we still dealing with social status?

148
00:14:00,352 --> 00:14:01,660
People are supposed to be equal nowadays.

149
00:14:02,683 --> 00:14:03,840
Equal, huh?

150
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,240
They just have more money than us.

151
00:14:12,696 --> 00:14:15,102
I’ve got money too. Why should I back down?

152
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,841
This school belongs to Tokyo.

153
00:14:29,768 --> 00:14:30,920
Who’s part of this crew?

154
00:14:54,326 --> 00:14:56,520
I heard there’s a new girl. Who is she?

155
00:14:56,747 --> 00:14:59,640
You’ll know soon. Someone is already giving her a proper welcome.

156
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,441
[Kongpurim]

157
00:15:01,955 --> 00:15:03,480
Go ahead and leave your phone here.

158
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,841
Then you can introduce yourself to everyone.

159
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:13,921
Hello, everyone.

160
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:15,201
My name is Blue,

161
00:15:15,860 --> 00:15:17,200
Phakjira Monchaitrakul.

162
00:15:22,563 --> 00:15:25,200
Once you’ve introduced yourself, take the desk in the back.

163
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:27,761
Right there.

164
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:28,961
Hey, everyone.

165
00:15:29,238 --> 00:15:31,680
Finish your homework, okay? I’ll come back and check it later.

166
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,200
You’re in my seat. Move.

167
00:15:40,846 --> 00:15:41,960
And this one is mine.

168
00:15:45,726 --> 00:15:48,840
Oh, so you're Zai and Pupe.

169
00:15:50,144 --> 00:15:51,642
Tokyo's lapdogs.

170
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:54,080
There is no reason to be rude.

171
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,320
Are you trying to pick a fight with me?

172
00:15:57,696 --> 00:16:00,240
Didn’t your parents teach you any manners?

173
00:16:01,296 --> 00:16:02,297
They did.

174
00:16:02,774 --> 00:16:04,640
They taught me to save them for people who deserve them.

175
00:16:07,302 --> 00:16:09,160
You two went through my bag last night, didn’t you?

176
00:16:09,728 --> 00:16:10,729
What's wrong with you?

177
00:16:11,035 --> 00:16:12,840
What are you talking about? We didn't do it.

178
00:16:14,048 --> 00:16:15,280
You did it, so own up to it.

179
00:16:15,355 --> 00:16:17,680
I told you I didn’t do it. What’s wrong with you?

180
00:16:31,974 --> 00:16:32,975
Hey!

181
00:16:35,499 --> 00:16:36,500
What the hell?

182
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:49,049
Oh,

183
00:16:50,352 --> 00:16:51,353
it's you.

184
00:16:52,667 --> 00:16:54,040
You're new here, at least you should learn

185
00:16:55,174 --> 00:16:56,460
how things are done around here.

186
00:16:57,296 --> 00:16:58,297
Why?

187
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:00,600
Since when do you have to be a gangster just to sit in class?

188
00:17:01,566 --> 00:17:03,200
- A gangster?
- I'm talking about you?

189
00:17:05,187 --> 00:17:06,520
You know me that well, huh?

190
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:08,240
Enough to call me a gangster?

191
00:17:09,909 --> 00:17:12,000
You’ve got your name plastered all over the building.

192
00:17:12,472 --> 00:17:13,480
You’d have to be an idiot not to know.

193
00:17:16,573 --> 00:17:18,120
I heard your dad’s such a big shot?

194
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:22,400
Don’t forget, he’s not the one sitting in class.

195
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:28,120
Where am I allowed to sit?

196
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,640
Sit wherever you want.

197
00:17:32,283 --> 00:17:33,720
There are plenty of empty seats.

198
00:17:34,352 --> 00:17:36,200
Just don’t sit in someone else’s seat.

199
00:17:36,251 --> 00:17:37,252
Yeah?

200
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,560
So, does that mean I can sit on your head?

201
00:17:43,294 --> 00:17:44,295
Can you stop being a smart-ass?

202
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,721
I told you, sit wherever you want,

203
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:49,280
as long as it’s not someone else’s seat.

204
00:17:52,910 --> 00:17:55,320
Holy shit, someone’s actually standing up to Tokyo.

205
00:17:59,808 --> 00:18:00,809
Hey!

206
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:02,921
What is going on over there?

207
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:08,480
Phakjira, you still haven’t found a seat?

208
00:18:09,110 --> 00:18:11,720
I told you to sit over there, next to Zai’s desk.

209
00:18:16,504 --> 00:18:19,120
Nice. Making trouble on your first day already.

210
00:18:19,811 --> 00:18:20,883
I didn't start it.

211
00:18:20,896 --> 00:18:21,997
You’re still talking back?

212
00:18:34,312 --> 00:18:35,313
Tokyo, dear.

213
00:18:36,152 --> 00:18:38,800
The English literature board in the library isn’t finished yet, is it?

214
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:42,401
I think I’ve found someone to do it for you.

215
00:19:21,576 --> 00:19:22,723
Hello, Captain Big.

216
00:19:22,872 --> 00:19:25,120
Hello, were you here to see my dad?

217
00:19:25,206 --> 00:19:27,120
I thought I’d stop by for some good luck before I go gambling today.

218
00:19:27,224 --> 00:19:29,400
Hopefully, luck will be on my side.

219
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:30,801
- I should go.
- Okay.

220
00:19:43,291 --> 00:19:44,560
How was your trip to Singapore?

221
00:19:44,923 --> 00:19:45,924
It was nice.

222
00:19:53,992 --> 00:19:55,320
We made it just in time to submit our bid.

223
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:57,840
These are just the backup ones, Dad.

224
00:19:58,603 --> 00:20:01,060
I already gave the main batch to Chief Tul’s men before I came home.

225
00:20:04,806 --> 00:20:07,424
We managed to pull the money from the Singapore account first this time,

226
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:12,800
but if we let Yi keep operating it,

227
00:20:14,856 --> 00:20:16,600
the numbers will keep sinking further into the red.

228
00:20:19,472 --> 00:20:20,473
Big, you ass hole.

229
00:20:20,502 --> 00:20:21,720
You’re a captain, for crying out loud.

230
00:20:21,744 --> 00:20:23,160
Can’t you handle something this small?

231
00:20:23,968 --> 00:20:25,776
Are you letting patrol cops raid the gambling den every day?

232
00:20:25,867 --> 00:20:27,080
How am I supposed to make any profit?

233
00:20:27,808 --> 00:20:29,210
Fuck, I’m already handling it.

234
00:20:30,304 --> 00:20:32,760
Those guys are just doing a routine inspection to keep the locals from complaining.

235
00:20:34,726 --> 00:20:36,280
The gambling den isn’t what’s losing money--

236
00:20:37,819 --> 00:20:39,480
our family’s going under because of your boxing camp.

237
00:20:40,326 --> 00:20:42,000
You’re always paying everything for your men.

238
00:20:43,616 --> 00:20:45,040
Yi made the right call.

239
00:20:46,544 --> 00:20:48,280
The boxing camp is there to support my men.

240
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:51,049
And when you run in the next election,

241
00:20:52,294 --> 00:20:55,120
you’ll be relying on all these people to act as your vote canvassers.

242
00:20:56,539 --> 00:20:57,540
Dad,

243
00:20:58,427 --> 00:21:00,160
I can quit and help with the family's business.

244
00:21:01,475 --> 00:21:02,476
No need to.

245
00:21:03,491 --> 00:21:04,800
Yi can handle everything.

246
00:21:06,323 --> 00:21:08,560
I’ve planned everything out for you.

247
00:21:09,264 --> 00:21:10,880
All you have to do is follow the plan.

248
00:21:13,774 --> 00:21:14,775
Dad?

249
00:21:16,195 --> 00:21:17,760
Did you plan everything out for Tokyo?

250
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:21,082
Let’s worry about getting her to wake up for school first.

251
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:24,660
Can’t you two even take care

252
00:21:25,499 --> 00:21:26,720
of your little sister?

253
00:21:37,435 --> 00:21:38,436
Yes, Uncle.

254
00:21:41,307 --> 00:21:42,308
Got it.

255
00:21:44,952 --> 00:21:45,960
What's the matter?

256
00:21:47,928 --> 00:21:49,920
Somboon said there was a problem with the bid submission.

257
00:21:59,059 --> 00:22:00,520
A new bidder competed against us

258
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:02,481
and they got the contract.

259
00:22:03,550 --> 00:22:04,551
Who's that?

260
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:08,121
It's Monchaitrakul.

261
00:22:40,134 --> 00:22:43,120
Ms. Paew from Class 6/3 sent me to help with the bulletin board.

262
00:22:43,456 --> 00:22:44,960
Oh, you're the new girl.

263
00:22:45,179 --> 00:22:46,640
Ms. Paew told me about you.

264
00:22:46,939 --> 00:22:50,000
Nothing much. You can just decorating the library bulletin board.

265
00:22:50,571 --> 00:22:54,080
The topic can be anything related to classic literature.

266
00:22:54,763 --> 00:22:57,880
You can find the materials yourself—whatever works for you.

267
00:23:06,384 --> 00:23:07,385
What?

268
00:23:07,670 --> 00:23:09,136
Why are you still here?

269
00:23:09,387 --> 00:23:12,040
You’ve got just three days to put the bulletin board together, sweetie.

270
00:23:12,459 --> 00:23:13,460
Three days.

271
00:23:13,510 --> 00:23:14,511
Move along.

272
00:24:00,344 --> 00:24:01,480
You scared me!

273
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:04,080
Can't you just come in properly?

274
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:07,480
There's one left, I haven't--

275
00:27:09,560 --> 00:27:11,720
[Throw this away for me. I have to run.]

276
00:27:15,261 --> 00:27:16,262
Bitch.

277
00:27:26,440 --> 00:27:27,845
Ms. Tokyo, you can park here.

278
00:27:27,976 --> 00:27:29,760
It's okay. I can park in the back.

279
00:27:45,003 --> 00:27:46,004
See?

280
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:47,960
I’m not some gangster like you assumed.

281
00:27:51,675 --> 00:27:53,920
Yeah? What is that?

282
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,480
[Love until our last breath]

283
00:28:21,899 --> 00:28:24,500
[Willing to die for love]

284
00:28:41,048 --> 00:28:42,049
So cringe.

285
00:28:43,275 --> 00:28:44,800
Who the hell would die for love?

286
00:28:48,160 --> 00:28:49,361
They call it a classic.

287
00:28:54,214 --> 00:28:55,440
Can you help--

288
00:29:07,384 --> 00:29:08,385
Hey.

289
00:29:08,718 --> 00:29:10,040
If you’re going to come here and not help,

290
00:29:10,872 --> 00:29:12,000
don’t bother coming next time.

291
00:29:19,043 --> 00:29:20,320
You can't fool me twice.

292
00:29:21,299 --> 00:29:22,360
You think I'm that stupid?

293
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:26,243
This isn’t trash.

294
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:28,401
I brought you some chips.

295
00:30:04,768 --> 00:30:07,611
Ju..Julite?

296
00:30:07,832 --> 00:30:10,240
It’s spelled J-U-L-I-E-T, not J-U-L-I-T-E.

297
00:30:12,027 --> 00:30:13,040
Did you type that wrong?

298
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:21,881
Hey!

299
00:30:24,488 --> 00:30:25,489
it's Juliet.

300
00:30:43,979 --> 00:30:44,980
Your drawings are really good.

301
00:30:46,360 --> 00:30:47,761
Do you ever take commissions?

302
00:30:48,838 --> 00:30:49,839
Nope.

303
00:30:50,550 --> 00:30:51,560
They're for my eyes only.

304
00:30:53,070 --> 00:30:54,480
What? What do you mean?

305
00:30:54,707 --> 00:30:57,480
Your skills are good enough to compete with artists from all over the world.

306
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:03,761
- Hey.
- Hey.

307
00:31:06,491 --> 00:31:08,280
Why are you talking to me? What do you want?

308
00:31:09,102 --> 00:31:10,880
You’re already listed as part of the group anyway.

309
00:31:11,795 --> 00:31:13,120
I saw you working alone,

310
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:15,480
so I came over to keep you company.

311
00:31:16,971 --> 00:31:18,080
I don't want your company.

312
00:31:22,120 --> 00:31:23,660
I don’t want to be part of a group…

313
00:31:24,121 --> 00:31:26,200
with a lame-ass name like “Street Queens.”

314
00:31:26,646 --> 00:31:27,647
What?

315
00:31:31,131 --> 00:31:32,132
What's the name again?

316
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:33,561
Street Queens, isn't it?

317
00:31:37,840 --> 00:31:38,841
Are you insane?

318
00:31:40,040 --> 00:31:41,646
Who would call themselves “Street Queens”?

319
00:31:43,059 --> 00:31:45,800
We didn’t name ourselves that. Our classmates did.

320
00:31:46,560 --> 00:31:47,600
Street Queens, really?

321
00:31:54,496 --> 00:31:55,497
Hey,

322
00:31:57,240 --> 00:31:58,320
are you still mad?

323
00:32:02,755 --> 00:32:04,880
About what you said about someone going through your things—

324
00:32:05,422 --> 00:32:07,200
we didn't do it.

325
00:32:08,854 --> 00:32:09,855
The same goes for the seats.

326
00:32:10,230 --> 00:32:12,360
Those seats really belonged to Zai and Pupe.

327
00:32:13,462 --> 00:32:14,480
We didn’t do it.

328
00:32:15,888 --> 00:32:17,240
About the classmates,

329
00:32:19,366 --> 00:32:20,840
you transferred here in 12th grade,

330
00:32:22,267 --> 00:32:23,600
so they’re probably just curious.

331
00:32:24,475 --> 00:32:25,640
You showed up out of nowhere.

332
00:32:26,822 --> 00:32:28,320
You could’ve just asked

333
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:30,520
instead of bullying someone

334
00:32:30,691 --> 00:32:32,280
and expecting them to treat you well.

335
00:32:37,710 --> 00:32:40,260
I transferred here to apply through the art program’s quota.

336
00:32:58,920 --> 00:33:01,440
Why didn't you use the bandage I gave you?

337
00:33:03,510 --> 00:33:04,560
Oh, it's nothing.

338
00:33:07,078 --> 00:33:08,079
It's not nothing.

339
00:33:11,542 --> 00:33:12,543
Turn and face me.

340
00:34:20,958 --> 00:34:21,959
What?

341
00:34:22,683 --> 00:34:24,240
DaouOffroad will be here?

342
00:34:25,160 --> 00:34:27,161
Let me see.

343
00:34:30,243 --> 00:34:31,560
It's not far from here.

344
00:34:32,720 --> 00:34:33,721
We should go.

345
00:34:35,808 --> 00:34:36,840
How could we go?

346
00:34:37,757 --> 00:34:39,360
I’m not allowed to leave the dorm at night.

347
00:34:41,005 --> 00:34:42,010
Of course, you can.

348
00:34:42,840 --> 00:34:43,841
You can just walk.

349
00:34:45,651 --> 00:34:46,652
Look,

350
00:34:46,894 --> 00:34:48,400
I’m not some big shot like you.

351
00:34:49,290 --> 00:34:51,060
I can’t just go wherever I want without getting in trouble.

352
00:35:09,736 --> 00:35:10,737
Get up.

353
00:35:11,660 --> 00:35:13,320
Where are we going? The work isn’t finished yet.

354
00:35:14,360 --> 00:35:15,760
To go see your favorite duo.

355
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:21,560
You're with the big shot.

356
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:23,081
No one’s gonna say anything.

357
00:35:37,995 --> 00:35:39,160
Aren’t you the big shot?

358
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:41,560
Why can’t we just get me out through the front gate?

359
00:35:41,734 --> 00:35:42,760
Actually, we can.

360
00:35:43,595 --> 00:35:45,760
But I don't want my dad's guys to know where I am.

361
00:35:46,134 --> 00:35:47,135
I don't like it.

362
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:49,720
Nepo baby, for real.

363
00:35:56,774 --> 00:35:58,120
- Are you serious?
- Yeah.

364
00:36:01,704 --> 00:36:02,960
You go first.

365
00:36:03,646 --> 00:36:04,647
- Are you sure it's safe?
- Of course.

366
00:36:09,571 --> 00:36:10,572
Get up there.

367
00:36:22,584 --> 00:36:23,585
You good?

368
00:36:23,760 --> 00:36:24,761
- Yeah.
- Catch this.

369
00:36:28,584 --> 00:36:29,585
One more.

370
00:36:45,179 --> 00:36:46,600
Can we wear this inside?

371
00:36:47,008 --> 00:36:48,060
And we're still underage.

372
00:36:48,880 --> 00:36:50,110
Hello, Tokyo.

373
00:36:50,579 --> 00:36:52,120
Your brother is not here with you?

374
00:36:52,840 --> 00:36:53,841
I'm here with my friend.

375
00:36:54,542 --> 00:36:56,600
I’ll have someone save two seats for you.

376
00:37:03,675 --> 00:37:05,480
Please put on your jackets.

377
00:37:24,022 --> 00:37:25,060
Are you alright?

378
00:37:26,680 --> 00:37:27,760
We're here now, aren't we?

379
00:37:28,480 --> 00:37:30,560
I wonder what it’s like

380
00:37:30,581 --> 00:37:31,660
to live with powerful connections.

381
00:37:36,571 --> 00:37:37,572
Welcome.

382
00:38:13,395 --> 00:38:16,640
Wow, mob boss’s daughters still exist these days?

383
00:38:18,509 --> 00:38:19,510
They still exist.

384
00:38:20,344 --> 00:38:22,720
We just don’t call them mob bosses anymore.

385
00:38:23,312 --> 00:38:25,440
These days, we call them…

386
00:38:26,075 --> 00:38:27,120
“powerful figures.”

387
00:38:28,507 --> 00:38:30,060
Whoa, powerful figures.

388
00:38:34,512 --> 00:38:35,520
What happened to that wound?

389
00:38:36,680 --> 00:38:38,480
Who did you get into a fight with?

390
00:38:40,619 --> 00:38:41,620
You mean this?

391
00:38:46,531 --> 00:38:47,560
I don't remember.

392
00:38:47,992 --> 00:38:49,260
You've been in a lot of fights.

393
00:38:51,800 --> 00:38:53,046
Yeah, quite a lot.

394
00:38:53,510 --> 00:38:55,680
But it’s not what you think.

395
00:38:56,203 --> 00:38:57,204
Well…

396
00:38:57,814 --> 00:39:00,080
Dad said I was really stubborn when I was younger.

397
00:39:00,459 --> 00:39:02,520
I used to wander around all the time,

398
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:04,360
and then I fell down the stairs.

399
00:39:07,312 --> 00:39:09,320
Don’t tell anyone.

400
00:39:09,643 --> 00:39:11,120
You'll lose you mob boss’s daughter credit.

401
00:39:12,760 --> 00:39:13,960
I’ve never told anyone.

402
00:39:17,368 --> 00:39:20,110
I haven't done anything as impressive as you think.

403
00:39:21,038 --> 00:39:22,600
I'm just a normal girl.

404
00:39:24,686 --> 00:39:25,687
Not true.

405
00:39:26,547 --> 00:39:29,200
At least, your family is wealthy.

406
00:39:30,536 --> 00:39:31,920
So, your name's Tokyo.

407
00:39:33,427 --> 00:39:34,560
Were you born in Tokyo?

408
00:39:37,374 --> 00:39:38,375
Nope.

409
00:39:41,550 --> 00:39:42,920
I was named after my dad’s favorite snack, a Thai treat called “Tokyo.”

410
00:39:50,080 --> 00:39:51,081
What's the filling?

411
00:39:52,291 --> 00:39:53,920
I don't know. You have to ask him.

412
00:39:54,152 --> 00:39:55,260
Nope.

413
00:39:56,200 --> 00:39:58,320
I asked you—what’s the filling?

414
00:40:03,299 --> 00:40:04,300
What's the filling?

415
00:40:06,860 --> 00:40:08,440
Good...feelings.

416
00:40:13,176 --> 00:40:14,520
Fine. Good feelings it is.

417
00:40:17,006 --> 00:40:18,680
Which one do you recommend, local expert?

418
00:40:19,880 --> 00:40:21,320
I haven’t tried them either.

419
00:40:23,037 --> 00:40:24,360
I’ll get whatever you get.

420
00:40:26,488 --> 00:40:27,489
Hello.

421
00:40:31,070 --> 00:40:32,160
We'd like to order this one.

422
00:40:32,616 --> 00:40:33,617
You got it.

423
00:40:55,062 --> 00:40:56,063
You think it'd help?

424
00:41:29,694 --> 00:41:30,695
Cheers!

425
00:41:41,995 --> 00:41:42,996
Don’t your mom and dad miss you

426
00:41:43,883 --> 00:41:45,280
after you moved here?

427
00:41:48,646 --> 00:41:49,647
Well…

428
00:41:49,984 --> 00:41:52,920
consider it practice for college life in Bangkok.

429
00:41:53,214 --> 00:41:58,960
Are you that confident you’ll get in?

430
00:41:59,216 --> 00:42:00,217
Wait,

431
00:42:01,297 --> 00:42:04,280
weren’t you the one

432
00:42:04,790 --> 00:42:06,240
who said I draw well?

433
00:42:11,469 --> 00:42:12,960
Yes, I like your drawings.

434
00:42:14,755 --> 00:42:16,520
You’re going to get in through the art quota anyway.

435
00:42:17,680 --> 00:42:18,681
That's right.

436
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:21,382
I will get in.

437
00:42:35,065 --> 00:42:38,240
♪ Hey, is the world ♪

438
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:42,800
♪ still not hot enough for you? ♪

439
00:42:44,464 --> 00:42:47,480
♪ Everything you do ♪

440
00:42:47,696 --> 00:42:52,200
♪ just drives the temperature higher. ♪

441
00:42:52,475 --> 00:42:56,160
♪ Every move you make, every look you give, ♪

442
00:42:56,251 --> 00:42:58,800
♪ drives me crazy.♪

443
00:42:59,408 --> 00:43:04,000
♪ No matter how hard I try, I can’t resist you. ♪

444
00:43:08,840 --> 00:43:13,660
♪ The temperature of my heart is out of control. ♪

445
00:43:15,998 --> 00:43:19,800
♪ You set me burning, burning, burning inside—♪

446
00:43:20,360 --> 00:43:22,260
♪ Teasing, till my heart melts.♪

447
00:43:22,480 --> 00:43:24,810
♪ My heats is melting and melting.♪

448
00:43:24,840 --> 00:43:27,560
♪ I’m ready for you to burn my body and soul.♪

449
00:43:32,990 --> 00:43:35,200
♪ You're melting my heart.♪

450
00:43:36,540 --> 00:43:39,760
♪ My heats is melting and melting.♪

451
00:43:42,400 --> 00:43:44,600
♪ You're melting my heart.♪

452
00:43:50,443 --> 00:43:51,444
Hey!

453
00:44:02,891 --> 00:44:04,640
Oh, I threw up all over your shirt.

454
00:44:05,558 --> 00:44:07,440
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

455
00:44:07,877 --> 00:44:08,878
That's fine.

456
00:44:10,694 --> 00:44:11,695
It's a mess.

457
00:44:12,005 --> 00:44:14,400
It's totally fine. It's alright.

458
00:44:15,720 --> 00:44:16,721
Let's have a seat.

459
00:44:18,582 --> 00:44:20,200
Watch out! Walk slowly.

460
00:44:38,360 --> 00:44:40,480
Your name is Tokyo

461
00:44:41,235 --> 00:44:42,720
because you like to visit Japan?

462
00:44:44,874 --> 00:44:46,120
You asked me that already.

463
00:44:47,854 --> 00:44:49,320
I was named after Dad's favorite snack.

464
00:44:52,328 --> 00:44:53,560
That's so funny.

465
00:44:55,774 --> 00:44:56,920
What's your favorite filling?

466
00:44:58,600 --> 00:44:59,601
The sweet ones.

467
00:45:05,280 --> 00:45:06,320
I'll get some for you.

468
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:09,001
What?

469
00:45:10,680 --> 00:45:12,560
- You're buying me snacks?
- Yeah.

470
00:45:15,803 --> 00:45:17,160
I want to pay you back.

471
00:45:21,184 --> 00:45:22,185
Yeah?

472
00:45:34,810 --> 00:45:35,811
Can I ask you something?

473
00:45:38,062 --> 00:45:39,063
What?

474
00:45:43,960 --> 00:45:45,061
Can we be friends now?

475
00:45:51,891 --> 00:45:52,892
Yeah.

476
00:46:01,723 --> 00:46:02,840
So we're friends now.

477
00:46:21,699 --> 00:46:22,700
Am I heavy?

478
00:46:22,980 --> 00:46:24,981
Of course you are. What kind of question is that?

479
00:46:33,979 --> 00:46:35,880
Do I need to carry you all the way to your room?

480
00:46:37,781 --> 00:46:38,782
You don't have to.

481
00:46:39,056 --> 00:46:40,880
Okay, I should go.

482
00:46:41,520 --> 00:46:42,521
See you tomorrow.

483
00:46:42,600 --> 00:46:44,360
Hey, hold on.

484
00:46:44,672 --> 00:46:45,673
What?

485
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:47,001
Stay right here.

486
00:46:54,077 --> 00:46:55,078
What is it?

487
00:47:00,035 --> 00:47:01,440
Have you finished the library bulletin board?

488
00:47:28,060 --> 00:47:30,210
Actually, you don't have to give me your shirt.

489
00:47:30,580 --> 00:47:31,800
[Sinittha Kongpurim]

490
00:47:31,894 --> 00:47:32,895
You can't.

491
00:47:33,160 --> 00:47:34,960
How can you wear it when it’s covered in my puke?

492
00:47:35,195 --> 00:47:36,200
Let me wash it first.

493
00:47:38,760 --> 00:47:39,761
Okay.

494
00:47:40,285 --> 00:47:41,660
Then make sure you use fabric softener, too.

495
00:47:42,774 --> 00:47:43,880
I know.

496
00:47:44,891 --> 00:47:46,200
Alright, see you later.

497
00:47:46,448 --> 00:47:47,449
See ya.

498
00:48:02,062 --> 00:48:05,200
This is what happens to anyone

499
00:48:05,576 --> 00:48:06,920
who sells the Kongpurims’ information to the other side.

500
00:48:11,741 --> 00:48:14,400
Mr. Po, please. Give me another chance.

501
00:48:14,880 --> 00:48:16,840
You asked for another chance?

502
00:48:17,240 --> 00:48:18,241
I'm not giving it to you.

503
00:48:20,645 --> 00:48:21,646
Yi?

504
00:48:27,501 --> 00:48:28,502
How are you, honey?

505
00:48:29,774 --> 00:48:31,400
You're home late.

506
00:48:39,707 --> 00:48:42,240
Anyone who has anything to do with the Monchaitrakul family

507
00:48:43,600 --> 00:48:46,000
is not allowed to set foot in Kongpurim house.

508
00:48:52,960 --> 00:48:54,961
[Monchaitrakul]

509
00:49:08,923 --> 00:49:11,240
What do you think of the Monchaitrakul girl?

510
00:49:12,920 --> 00:49:14,200
It’s got a sweet filling, just like I promised.

511
00:49:15,680 --> 00:49:17,160
I come from the Kongpurim family.

512
00:49:17,694 --> 00:49:19,700
I would never associate with a Monchaitrakul.

513
00:49:20,400 --> 00:49:21,720
Do you know who did this?

514
00:49:21,971 --> 00:49:23,120
I need to know who to go after.

515
00:49:24,720 --> 00:49:28,000
If the Monchaitrakul and Kongpurim families went to war,
who do you think would win?

516
00:49:29,725 --> 00:49:30,726
Actually,

517
00:49:31,176 --> 00:49:33,040
we shouldn't have been friends.

518
00:49:33,040 --> 00:49:34,040
MkvDrama.net

